Resists are pretty important...<BR>Fire and Magic<P>So...for our guilds, having a few bards is key.  Pre-Kunark the Uber-Guilds had Naggy/Vox down to a 3 group formula...but that was with everyone 50th lvl in full planes gear.  <P>I think we can manage 3 bards right now...pretty good for the key groups...maybe 4 bards pumping MR/FR/CR for their groups.<P>Prae folks and Div13 folks really don't mind a defeat or two...it's the other people that we would need to add to fill our ranks that I'd be worried about.  Too many people play this game with a total fear of death.  We can't do that without X-Y-Z...whaaa.  Makes me sick sometimes.<P>OSW has a few in the right level range right now....so there might be some people to get from there.  <P>We'd also need to be ready to go within a few hours notice.  Since Naggy/Vox isn't a reservable spawn like Hate/Fear/Sky...makes it harder to plan what is essentially a pickup raid.<P>Me..personally...I'm optimistic or stupid enought to think that with 3-4 bards and a cleric for each group with enough tanks and blasters...we could do it with 3 ( lucky ) or 4 groups.  The key would be the tanks staying alive and maintaining aggro...then enough nukers to blast it down fast once it was past 50% or so.  <P>Naggy would be my pick for a first dragon raid due to 1) Naggy does not CH & 2) SolB is easy to get too.<P>We can zone in with the raid team...and even if Naggy not up..we can do the fire giants.  A good dry run so to speak.  Our high levels can help here and then if Naggy is up..keep them off the Dragon teams while we buff up and give it a try.  If we fail, then rezz and assess the situation...try again if it looks doable with a few tweaks.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>--------------------<P>Sleethr - 54th DE Mage<BR>Medec - 42nd level Battle Cleric<BR>Meekka - 33rd DE Rogue<BR>Vowk - 27th Dr00d
